! jb_af1c F213 "ADD TO EXPONENT TEST", sub-block F213C "TEST UNCHANGED
! REGISTERS", p.129 (octal 017245.00-017263.00, the block's own exit
! "BD,$+1.0").  This completes F213.
!
! Two sub-tests, the same shape as F212XC: set everything to a known
! value, run one E+, and ask that the parts E+ must not disturb came
! through.  p.102: "Accumulator bits 108-127 and the sign byte register
! remain unchanged."
!
!   C1  Z,$L / Z,$R / Z,$SB -- all zero -- then E+(U),FPK1.
!       "CHECK R44-63 REMAIN+0" and "CHECK SB0-7 REMAIN+0".
!   C2  C1111 both halves and CM1111 the sign byte -- all ones -- then
!       E+(U),FPK0.  "1 S REMAIN 1 S, R44-63 AND SB0-7".
!
! NOTE THE FULL SIGN BYTE, 0-7.  F212XC had to check F+'s sign byte in
! two pieces, 0-3 and 5-7, because bit 4 is the result sign and F+
! rewrites it.  E+ touches the sign not at all -- it adds exponents and
! "the fraction and sign of the addressed operands are ignored" -- so
! this block checks all eight bits in one connective.
!
! BOTH SUB-TESTS TAKE THE FLAGGED PATH, from opposite sides, which is
! worth knowing since neither comment says so:
!   C1 zeroes the accumulator (exponent 0, N range) and addresses
!      FPK1, all ones, whose exponent field is 2047 with ES 1 -- XFN.
!      So Figure 32 gives the MEMORY operand's exponent.
!   C2 fills the accumulator with ones, which makes ITS exponent field
!      2047 with ES 1 -- also XFN -- and addresses FPK0, exponent 0 in
!      the N range, so the ACCUMULATOR's exponent survives.
! Neither checks the exponent; what they check is that the fraction's
! low twenty bits and the sign byte are untouched either way.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes: SERS (octal 1304) -> FAIL halt,
! -- SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch.
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --
        SLC, (8)22005.0
FPK0    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000000000000000000000
FPK1    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777777777777777777777

        SLC, (8)17245.0
FAE4    Z, $L                                ! F213C1 - R44-63 and SB0-7 remain 0
        Z, $R
        Z, $SB
        E+(U), FPK1
        CT0101(BU,20), FPK0                  ! check R44-63 remain +0
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT0011(BU,8), $SB                    ! check SB0-7 remain +0
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32                             ! F213C2 - 1 s remain 1 s, R44-63 and SB0-7
        C1111(BU,64), FPK1, 64
        C1111(BU,64), FPK1
        CM1111(BU,8), $SB
        E+(U), FPK0
        CT1010(BU,20), FPK1                  ! check R44-63 remain +1 s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT1100(BU,8), $SB                    ! check SB0-7 remain +1 s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                               ! 017263.00: the block's exit "BD,$+1.0"
        END, FAE4
